# Build context filter for server/app/ai-service/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile's dev and prod stages both do `COPY . .` after `uv sync`.
# Without this file that copy undoes two deliberate design decisions and leaks
# a credential:
#
#   - models/*.onnx, *.npz, *.pt — ADR-005: the image ships NO weights. They
#     are downloaded from R2 by docker-entrypoint.sh on first start, sha256'd
#     against the baked-in manifest, and cached on a volume. A local checkout
#     that has run `fetch_models.py` holds ~78 MB of them plus crnn.pt, and
#     `COPY . .` would bake all of it into every layer — while the entrypoint
#     re-downloads them anyway.
#   - .venv — created by `uv sync` on the *host*. It contains absolute paths
#     and platform-specific wheels (onnxruntime, opencv), and `COPY . .` lands
#     after the image's own `uv sync`, so the host copy wins. The failure is at
#     import time in the container, not at build time.
#   - .env — a real credential, baked into an image layer and travelling with
#     it forever.
#
# The root .dockerignore does NOT cover this build. It applies to the `web`
# image, which is the only one whose context is the repository root.
#
# models/EXPECTED_HASHES.json is NOT excluded and must not be: it is the
# manifest the entrypoint reads to know what to download and what the bytes
# should hash to, and the Dockerfile copies it explicitly before this stage.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# Model weights — fetched from R2 at runtime, never baked in. See ADR-005.
models/*.onnx
models/*.npz
models/*.pt

# Dev-only debug output from AI_DEBUG_DUMP_ENABLED=1. Never in an image.
debug_images

.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode

*.log
.DS_Store
